    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "you look at a wide variety. industries today, more and more Americans see them as being dominated by just a few very, very large firms. This is something we're really trying to push back on in Washington, D.C. We're losing some of that depth in our communities because now there's a huge multinational firm that dominates retail perhaps or dominates media perhaps or dominates online platforms perhaps. We want to make sure that there still is this sense in America, not only that it's your local business that you're supporting, but that you too can start that local business and be that person in retail, that person online, that person right here in the radio booth. I want to make sure that this is a country of upward mobility. I want to make sure this is a country where there are small businesses in our communities.",
