    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "just became about pushing more eyeballs, making it stickier, getting that headline that grabs more people's clicks instead of promoting good, reliable, unbiased information. And the more that we continue to allow that to happen, the more that we're inculcating not someone with a company's view, but that individual journalist that's trying to move up, that's trying to get more clicks than somebody else that wants the more rancorous headline. We've got to make sure that we push back against that and get to an environment where people can get access to a wide variety of information and can get access to the real information, not the story as filtered by a particular journalist political view. It's unbelievable what I observe in Washington. And then what I hear about from the conventional media right here at home, right? It's very, very different, right? The things that should be talked about aren't talked about at all. And the things that they are focused on day in and day out and hammering are the things that are totally irrelevant to what the bigger problems are in Washington.",
