    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86305.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 60,
    "turn_text": "Look, as I travel across Johnson County, as I meet with constituents, as I talk with businesses, I talk with nonprofits, the same things come up. Right? Given what we saw on our televisions in July, in August, these terrible tragedies happening in Afghanistan, how can we trust this administration to properly vet these refugees and then properly secure the compound to ensure that we are not causing problems right here in our communities? That's what I hear every single day, right? Who's just want to welcome open arms, those that supported our troops abroad, those that supported America, but Given this administration's abysmal failure and execution on what they called a withdrawal, I think there are rightly concerned that the vetting process isn't complete, that isn't being done well, that the process to keep Americans safe, whether that's from a biological standpoint and some of the diseases, or from a safety and security standpoint, that that process isn't being undertaken with the diligence it needs to. That is what Americans concerned about. That's what Hoosiers and Johnson County are concerned about, and the right to be concerned about it. The execution of the quote unquote withdrawal was horrifying to watch, angering to every American, especially those that sacrificed over in Afghanistan. And I think they're right to wonder whether this administration can properly vet and handle the refugees that they've brought in.",
